<header><p class="st-kicker">tribal confederation · Poland, Lithuania and Russia</p><h1 class="st-title">Ilmen Slavs</h1><p class="st-meta">600 CE – 882 CE (approx.) · capital Novgorod</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The northernmost East Slavs, centred on Lake Ilmen, whose invitation to Rurik began the Rurikid dynasty in the chronicle tradition.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/slavs">Slavs</a> reached the basin of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lake-ilmen">Lake Ilmen</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/volkhov-river">Volkhov</a> river in the 7th and 8th centuries, settling among Finnic and Baltic peoples. The chronicles call them the Slovene. Their main centres were the trading settlement of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/staraya-ladoga">Staraya Ladoga</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rurikovo-gorodishche">Rurikovo Gorodishche</a> near the later <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/veliky-novgorod">Novgorod</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>They lived from farming, fishing, hunting and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fur-trade">fur trade</a>, and their territory sat on the routes linking the Baltic with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/volga">Volga</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dnieper">Dnieper</a>. Scandinavian merchants and warriors were present from the 8th century. The tribe was led by elders and assemblies, which foreshadowed the later town assembly, the veche, of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/veliky-novgorod">Novgorod</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>According to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/primary-chronicle">Primary Chronicle</a>, the Slovene, <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/krivichs">Krivichs</a> and Finnic tribes expelled the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/varangians">Varangians</a> and then invited <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rurik">Rurik</a> to rule them in 862. In 882 his successor Oleg moved south to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kyiv">Kiev</a>, and Ilmen became the northern half of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kievan-rus">Kievan Rus'</a>. Their land developed into the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/novgorod-republic">Novgorod Republic</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/ilmen-slavs.jpg" alt="Ilmen Slavs" width="320" height="489"><figcaption>Image: Лапоть · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Jewellery_Novgorod_Slovenes_GIM.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>600 CE – 882 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/7th-century">7th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/9th-century">9th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>tribal confederation</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Novgorod</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Rurik</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Slavic paganism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Old East Slavic</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/russia">Russia</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Ilmen Slovenes, Slovene of Novgorod</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=741&amp;focus=ilmen-slavs" aria-label="Ilmen Slavs on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5620 209 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Ilmen Slavs lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5940 465h0"/><path class="map-dot-ap" d="M5940 465h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>Location approximate: shown in present-day Russia. <a href="/atlas?year=741&amp;focus=ilmen-slavs">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
